<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project>

  <!--
    Build policy for the test suites, layered over the repository-wide file.

    The explicit Import is what makes this file a LAYER rather than a replacement: MSBuild stops at the
    nearest Directory.Build.props on the way up, so without it the root file's TargetFramework, Nullable and
    TreatWarningsAsErrors would silently stop applying to every project under tests/.

    The one property this layer changes is AnalysisMode, held at the SDK default while the rest of the
    repository runs at Recommended. What Recommended adds over Default is performance and API-shape rules —
    LoggerMessage delegates, concrete return types, sealed internal types, field-versus-property — aimed at
    an assembly that ships to someone. A test assembly ships nowhere: it is compiled, run once by the runner,
    and thrown away. Enforcing those rules here would rewrite test code to suit a shape it does not have.

    It is the mode alone that is lowered. The rules opted into by name in /.globalconfig — disposal,
    cancellation, dead conditions, structured logging — apply here exactly as they do everywhere else, and the
    ones that genuinely do not fit test code are turned off individually, with their reasons, in
    tests/.editorconfig.

    Be precise about what this DOES give up, because the list above does not include it: the CULTURE rules
    (CA1304/CA1305/CA1307/CA1309/CA1310/CA1311) are not opted into by name anywhere — they arrive with
    AnalysisMode, so lowering the mode switches them off for the suites. That is a real gap, not a covered
    one. The suites hand-manage culture instead (SetCulture attributes, explicit CultureInfo arguments), which
    is why a locale-dependent assertion is caught by review rather than by the compiler here. Opting the
    culture rules in by name is the way to close it, and it is a change with its own findings to fix first.
  -->
  <Import Project="$([MSBuild]::GetPathOfFileAbove('Directory.Build.props', '$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../'))" />

  <PropertyGroup>
    <AnalysisMode>Default</AnalysisMode>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
